{{!
    @template tool_vae/selfpos_hidden

    A record hidden under the vaeiste since the page was opened: the notice with the message of the record, then, when the
    vaeiste had typed more than blanks, a sentence and the text given back in a field that can be read and copied. A textarea
    keeps its text as it is written: nothing stands between its tags and the text.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\selfpos_hidden. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces) except one key:
    * messagehtml - the message of the record, a sentence of the language file whose title of the record was escaped by
      hidden_frameworks::message() (s()): placed as it is, as before, so that the title is escaped once

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * alertclass - string, the classes of the notice: information when nothing was sent, danger otherwise
    * messagehtml - string, the message of the record
    * kept - object or null: intro (the sentence), text (what was typed)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "alertclass": "alert alert-danger",
        "messagehtml": "The record Aide &amp; soins (RNCP100) is hidden.",
        "kept": {"intro": "Nothing has been recorded. Here is what you wrote.", "text": "Alone since the third week."}
    }
}}
<div class="{{alertclass}}">{{{messagehtml}}}</div>{{#kept}}<p>{{intro}}</p>{{!
}}<textarea readonly="readonly" rows="8" cols="70" class="form-control mb-3">{{text}}</textarea>{{/kept}}
